      "name": null,
      "problem": "The duration of a podcast episode is uniformly distributed between $25$ and $34$ minutes. What is the expected duration of an episode?",
      "worked_solution": "Let $X$ represent the duration of a randomly chosen episode. From the problem statement, we know that $X∼U[25,34],$ and we wish to compute $\\text{E}[X].$\n\nIn general, if $X∼U[a,b],$ then $X$ has the following expected value:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{a+b}{2}\n$$\n\nSo, for our random variable $X∼U[25,34],$ we have the following expected value:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{25+34}{2}=29.5\n$$\n\nTherefore, the mean duration of an episode is $29.5\\,\\text{min}.$",
